B = [
('HMT Watches','South Asia','1960s-1980s','watches','In the style of HMT Watches, modest, dependable, sentimental mid-century Indian craftsmanship. Small round or softly cushioned forms with thin bezels and plain backs, finished in polished steel or gold plating. Faces are simple and uncluttered in silver white, cream or sunburst gold, with slim baton markers, thin tapering gilt or steel pointers and a fine printed ring of tiny ticks. Lettering is neat serif capitals, small and evenly spaced. Details are restrained, with thin black or brown leather and plain steel fittings, and occasionally a glimpse of gears and gilded workings under clear plate. Packaging is modest card lined in blue velvet. Quiet, middle-class, gift-like and warmly nostalgic.'),
('Godrej','South Asia','1950s-1970s','furniture','In the style of Godrej, solid, heavy, trustworthy mid-century Indian steel furniture and appliances. Tall rectangular boxy volumes of welded sheet steel with rounded corners, heavy double doors, a single vertical chrome handle with a key lock and sometimes a full length mirror panel. Surfaces are thick baked enamel with a faint orange peel texture in grey green, olive, cream, rust brown, pale blue, dark green or black, with thin gold pinstripes on squat secure forms, brass hinges and a big round dial. Interiors are sturdy and practical. Badges and logos are looping cursive signature lettering in white, deep red or purple. Mood is secure, domestic, durable and post-independence.'),
('Rooh Afza','South Asia','1900s-present','drinks','In the style of Rooh Afza, rich, nostalgic, floral and festive South Asian label art. A vivid red field framed by a decorative border of small Mughal style flowers, with a central cartouche holding swashing Latin and Arabic script lettering in white and yellow. Surrounding illustrations of rose bunches, fruits, herbs and leaves are drawn in a fine old lithographic manner with delicate hatching. Glass is tall, square shouldered and slightly ribbed, filled with deep ruby colour and closed with red or gold caps. Colours are bright red, gold, deep green and cream, with warm red or pale pink backdrops. Cooling, sweet, perfumed, celebratory and heritage-rich.'),
('Khaadi','South Asia','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Khaadi, earthy, artisanal, modern-heritage handloom textiles. Loose, easy silhouettes in crisp matte cotton with a visible hand woven grain. Palette is mustard, indigo, rust, olive, ivory and deep red. Prints are bold block-print-inspired motifs, large paisleys, florals, small repeating geometry and interlocking patterns in two or three colours, set along hems and sleeves. Neat threadwork edges necklines and cuffs, with small mirrors, tassels and long striped scarves with fringed ends. Retail and photography feel airy, with warm wood, fabric rolls, soft beige and white walls and a small hand-drawn mark. Warm, cheerful and sunlit, as in an open courtyard.'),
('Pakistan International Airlines','South Asia','1960s-2010s','airlines','In the style of Pakistan International Airlines, dignified, proud, warm national livery design. A bright white upper body above a pale beige lower belly, divided by a dark green stripe edged in gold, with a large waving green and white flag on the tail. Names appear in big billboard capitals in dark green, backed by a flowing calligraphic script mark in gold. Special schemes borrow folk art such as blue and white floral tile decoration, fine tilework, bright needlework and bold red geometric woven motifs. Interiors use deep green with gold accents and patterned carpets. Green, white and gold glow against bright blue sky, with a thin red and green cheatline in early versions.'),
('Aarong','South Asia','1980s-present','retail','In the style of Aarong, rural, handmade, colourful and lovingly textured craft design. Handwoven cotton, silk and fine muslin in vivid turmeric yellow, red, indigo, leaf green and white, with block-printed borders, tiny woven floral motifs and fine stripes. The signature surface is quilted running-stitch embroidery forming flowers, fish, birds, trees and boats in rows of red, blue and green thread on white or black cloth, with a gentle wavy hand-stitched texture. Natural materials such as terracotta, jute, cane and brass add earthy warmth. Spaces are tall and bright with hanging fabrics, rustic wood, earthy walls and a gentle orange accent. Tags are cream paper with simple black type. Like a village fair in a tidy modern hall.'),
('Mysore Sandal Soap','South Asia','1960s-present','cosmetics','In the style of Mysore Sandal Soap, a treasured, perfumed, royal heritage gift look. Warm vermilion red, glossy gold and cream with sandy yellows, framed by an ornate border and a central heraldic mythical beast with a big curling mane, raised paws and a crown, drawn in a formal crest manner. Names are set in elegant serif capitals with a small line drawing of sandalwood leaves and flowers. Metallic gold paper with red printing wraps rectangular forms with softly rounded edges and a pressed emblem. Presentation feels like a gift, bound with a thin ribbon. Mood is traditional, calm, regal and sweetly fragrant, with glossy gold detail.'),
('Ashok Leyland','South Asia','1960s-1990s','vehicles','In the style of Ashok Leyland, rugged, colourful, overloaded, hand-decorated Indian heavy transport. Boxy upright forms with a flat vertical windscreen split in two, a plain rectangular grille with a horizontal chrome bar, wide round lamps and a high step. Paint is solid blue, red, yellow or cream, worn and faded, with thick hand painted borders, flower and peacock scenes, bold slogans in painted lettering and chequered stripes. Strings of lucky charms and tassels hang at the bumper. Bodies are rounded steel or fibreglass in faded red and cream with sliding windows with metal bars. Badge is a spoked wheel inside a circle. Gritty, dusty, golden hour mood.'),
('IndiGo','South Asia','2000s-present','airlines','In the style of IndiGo, clean, efficient, youthful and accessible modern identity in deep indigo blue. A white body with a large indigo area sweeping up toward the tail, a lighter sky blue accent stripe and small rounded lowercase lettering in indigo. The mark is built from a cluster of round dots arranged into a simple shape, in white or sky blue over indigo. Dark blue details carry tiny white text. Interiors are bright and simple in blue and white, with navy uniforms and an indigo belt. Printed material uses clear white backgrounds, a rich blue block and playful, crisp sans serif type. Cool, fresh and cheerful.'),
('Kingfisher Beer','South Asia','1980s-present','drinks','In the style of Kingfisher Beer, social, festive, glamorous hot-afternoon design with a bird emblem. Cream or white ground with a bold red band and a gold rim, a rounded top and strong upright serif capitals with a small crown icon. A bird in profile with a bright blue back, orange belly and long dark beak perches or dives above the name, drawn sleek and glossy. Slender brown glass and glossy cream and red surfaces are accented with gold rings and thick card details. Graphics turn bold red and white for sporting events. Warm red, gold, cream and a flash of electric blue, poolside and lively.'),
('Tiger Balm','Southeast Asia','1920s-present','cosmetics','In the style of Tiger Balm, vivid, nostalgic, bold medicinal packaging. Tiny faceted hexagonal or octagonal pots with bright red or white screw lids, tight wrap labels in red or white and small steel tins painted red and gold. The hero is a striding side-view big cat with a curved tail, drawn in an orange and black woodcut manner, set beside names in Latin and Chinese characters and tidy lines of tiny print. Cartons are vertical in red, yellow and green with an arc of text and a leaping central figure. Vintage posters use cartoon animals, hand lettering and a rich orange, yellow and black palette. Old pharmacy feel, pungent and strong.'),
('Proton','Southeast Asia','1980s-2000s','cars','In the style of Proton, proud, modest, practical, optimistic national design of the 1980s and 1990s. Compact, boxy, upright volumes with flat sides, a straight shoulder line, slim chrome bumpers, rectangular lamps and a plain black grille carrying a small badge. Badges are a dark blue shield with a yellow crescent and star, or a yellow tiger head in a green roundel. Paint is solid gloss in white, red, silver, dark blue and champagne gold, with black plastic window trim and simple wheel covers or slim five spoke alloys. Sloping roofs and low fronts appear on sportier shapes. Plain grey cloth interiors. Sunlit, with palm trees and low brick houses.'),
('Jollibee','Southeast Asia','1980s-present','food','In the style of Jollibee, joyful, loud, sweet, family-friendly fast food branding. A round-bodied cartoon mascot bee with a large head, big white eyes, a wide smile, small antennae, tiny wings, a red jacket and a white hat, and a fat black and yellow striped body in smooth glossy outline. The wordmark is chunky rounded red italic letters with a white outline and thick drop shadow on a bright yellow field. Spaces are red and yellow with big windows, shiny tables, plastic chairs, a play corner and staff in red shirts and caps. Packaging uses red paper boxes, white tubs and yellow sleeves. Very warm, cheerful and bright.'),
('Sarao Motors','Southeast Asia','1950s-1970s','vehicles','In the style of Sarao Motors, exuberant, crowded, festive, handmade vehicle design. A long boxy hand-beaten metal body on an army-surplus style chassis, with a long bonnet, two open facing benches, a rear step and a canopy roof. Every surface is covered in loud hand painted patterns such as stripes, checks, flames, flowers and animals, outlined in chrome strips, with abundant chrome decoration, small metal figures along the bonnet, tassels and many mirrors. Bold painted lettering carries slogans and names, with religious pictures above the driver. Interiors have polished rails, velvet or vinyl seats, fringes and mirrors. Saturated colour and heaps of chrome shining in the sun.'),
('Singha','Southeast Asia','1930s-present','drinks','In the style of Singha, sunny, tropical, festive heraldic design. A deep red and gold border frames a central mythical lion in a rearing pose with a curly mane, tufted tail, raised paw and fierce expression, drawn in old engraving style and flanked by ornamental curls, a crown emblem and a royal bird crest. The name sits below in bold upright capitals in gold or white. Surfaces are glossy deep red with gold and white detail and gold foil accents that add a sense of ceremony. Amber brown glass, brown and cream complete the palette. Photography shows chilled condensation beside spicy grilled food on banana leaf against a beach. Lively and bold.'),
('Garuda Indonesia','Southeast Asia','1980s-2000s','airlines','In the style of Garuda Indonesia, gracious, calm, tropical, island-like identity in deep blue and aqua. A clean white body with a swooping blue and turquoise stripe along the belly sweeping into a solid royal blue tail carrying a stylised bird emblem made from five bent lines like a spreading wing in aqua and white. The name is clean blue capitals in a wide, evenly spaced sans serif. An earlier scheme is red and white with a bright orange window stripe and a triangular bird. Interiors use soft blue seats, batik pattern head covers in brown and indigo, wood panels and gentle warm light. Crew wear fitted batik with a flower in the hair.'),
('Indomie','Southeast Asia','2000s-present','food','In the style of Indomie, hot, spicy, glossy, hungry, everyday and exuberant packaging. A flat glossy pouch in a bright red, orange and yellow gradient with white and gold sparkle, dominated by a big appetising photograph of stir fried noodles topped with a fried egg, shredded meat, cucumber, tomato and crisp shallots, with a drizzle of dark sweet sauce on a plain plate. The name is thick, rounded red and white lettering with a heavy black outline and a small flame or chilli. Variant colours such as blue, green and black code the flavours. Silver foil sachets and tall cups repeat the artwork. Street stall steam and boiling pots.'),
('Thai Airways','Southeast Asia','1990s-2010s','airlines','In the style of Thai Airways, graceful, silky, ornate and festive identity in orchid purple and gold. A white body with a sweeping band from nose to tail in shades of magenta, violet and gold, merging into a curved tail whose mark is a tall stylised flame-like roof curve built from gold and magenta. The name is a softly rounded italic sans serif in purple. Interiors use purple and orange seats, silk-like fabrics in orchid pink, patterned carpets and orchids on head rests. Crew wear silk wrap skirts and jackets in orchid purple, gold or magenta with a small flower corsage and a neat bun. Rich violet, magenta and gold, with classical dancers and royal barges for special schemes.'),
('Tiger Beer','Southeast Asia','1930s-present','drinks','In the style of Tiger Beer, cool, bold, energetic, nocturnal and urban design in navy, gold and hot orange. A deep navy label with a bold arched gold border, a leaping big cat in orange gold stripes on black rendered in dynamic ink lines, set above the name in big upright yellow capitals. A small crown, malt ears and a ribbon give a heraldic effect. Glossy navy surfaces with gold highlights and metallic silver. Marketing uses street art, bright orange, black and blue paint splashes, and stylised stripes across city scenes and festival stages. Ice buckets and red plastic tables at a night food market.'),
('Philippine Airlines','Southeast Asia','1990s-present','airlines','In the style of Philippine Airlines, bright, hospitable, tropical, crisp and patriotic identity built from sail-like triangles. A clean white body with the name in italic blue capitals, and a tail device of one blue triangle and one red triangle pointing like sails, with a small eight rayed yellow sun over the blue. A thin red and blue stripe runs near the windows, and engines stay plain white. Anniversary schemes use large stylised numbers. Interiors use deep blue seats with red piping and woven patterns, soft light and warm timber. Crew wear modern dresses in blue or red with traditional sleeves. Blue, red, white and sunny yellow.'),
('Pasabahce','Middle East','1960s-present','glassware','In the style of Pasabahce, hospitable, bright, tidy, sparkling domestic glassware with an Ottoman flavour. Small, slim, waisted forms with a flared lip and a gently pinched middle, clear and thin, set on little saucers. Larger pieces have cut and pressed patterns such as diamond facets, rosettes, fine vertical flutes and rows of tiny dots, with domed lids and tall necks. Coloured glass in cobalt blue, emerald green, amber and ruby red carries gilded rims and enamelled floral motifs of tulips, carnations and cypress in gold and white. Heavy rounded bases anchor tumblers. Glassy reflections, warm light, patterned cloth and brass in the background.'),
('Iran Khodro','Middle East','1970s-1990s','cars','In the style of Iran Khodro, humble, durable, nostalgic, lived-in practical mid-century design. Plain upright boxy bodies with a flat bonnet, a small rectangular grille with a horizontal bar, round or square chrome rimmed lamps and thin chrome bumpers. Paint is thick solid enamel in cream white, sky blue, pale yellow, red, green, bright orange or yellow, slightly faded, with black rubber seals, steel wheels with simple hub caps and white-wall style discs. Interiors are flat and plain in beige or brown with vinyl seats and a slim steering wheel. Seen in rows in dusty traffic below mountains. Communal and unfussy.'),
('Qatar Airways','Middle East','2000s-present','airlines','In the style of Qatar Airways, luxurious, formal, quiet, upmarket identity in burgundy and grey. A pale grey and white body with the name in large burgundy capitals, Arabic lettering nearby in a smaller darker grey, and a deep burgundy tail carrying a pale grey ring with a horned antelope silhouette. The finish is smooth and polished, with burgundy accents and a thin belly line. Interiors are stately in grey and burgundy leather, with private sliding-door suites and soft lighting. Lounges use marble floors, a huge sculpture and leather sofas. Crew wear deep maroon with a neat hat, veil and gold pin. Deep maroon, warm grey and a gleam of metal.'),
('Etihad Airways','Middle East','2010s-present','airlines','In the style of Etihad Airways, opulent, desert-warm, polished and glittering identity in sand and gold. A warm pale beige body, almost desert sand, with a triangular tessellation in gold and silver facets like a faceted gem across the tail and rear, fading toward the front. The name is a golden calligraphic mark above the windows. Interiors are sumptuous with beige and brown leather, gold trim, wood veneer and sliding doors. Crew wear fitted dark sand-coloured suits and a hat with a flowing scarf. Terminals use pale marble, golden light and sweeping curved roofs. A limited palette of gold, sand, taupe and white.'),
('El Al','Middle East','1970s-present','airlines','In the style of El Al, crisp, clean, secure, patriotic and cool identity in blue and white. A white body with a sweeping blue cheatline outlined in silver, running along the bottom, curving over the nose and fading toward the tail, with a plain white or blue tail and a flag. The name is a bold blue wordmark in Latin and a second script across the forward body. An older scheme uses a turquoise tail topped with a six pointed star and a turquoise and navy cheatline across the windows. Interiors use blue seats with white head covers, slim wood-look trim and blue and white carpets. Smart navy uniforms with pale blue blouses. Sunlit blue sky.'),
('SodaStream','Middle East','2010s-present','appliances','In the style of SodaStream, clean, modern, eco-minded, fresh and friendly home appliance design. Slim upright columns in black, white or brushed steel, with plain rounded tops, a clear push lever or button and a flat base. Clear or tinted tall flasks with slim necks and screw caps carry a fill line and a single coloured accent such as red, blue, green or bright orange. Slender gunmetal grey or lime green steel tanks add a small collar. Newer pared back forms in matte steel have a single dial. Syrup bottles are bright with flat labels in juicy colours. Imagery shows rising bubbles, fruit slices, ice and a bright white counter.'),
('Ararat Brandy','Middle East','1900s-present','drinks','In the style of Ararat Brandy, deep, aged, ceremonial and warm amber heritage design. Heavy glass with round shoulders and a long neck, closed with dark cork or a gilded stopper, filled with deep amber liquid. Labels are cream or ivory paper with a gold embossed border, a tall mountain with a snowy twin peak, strong serif capitals, an age numeral in a gold seal and a small vignette of a stone building. A red phoenix emblem appears on newer labels. Rows of little gold stars signal quality. Presentation cases are rich wood or velvet-lined with metal clasps. Rich brown, gold, burgundy and cream.'),
('Air Astana','Russia and Eastern Europe','2000s-present','airlines','In the style of Air Astana, orderly, formal, cool steppe-wide identity of dark blue and gold. A white body with a deep navy belly, a rich blue tail carrying a golden stylised ornament like a pair of wings or a nomadic motif, and gold lettering in a clean wide sans serif. Special schemes stretch a grey-spotted wild cat across the body with white and blue snowy rock. Interiors use navy seats patterned with ornamental motifs in gold thread, grey carpets and warm wood trim. Crew wear smart navy with gold buttons and silk scarves in a traditional pattern. Printed material repeats a navy field with a thin gold ornamental border, and carved screens and rugs echo it.'),
('Margilan Yodgorlik Silk Factory','Russia and Eastern Europe','traditional to present','textiles','In the style of Margilan Yodgorlik Silk Factory, vivid, sumptuous, handmade silky resist-dyed textiles. Lustrous silk is patterned by tying and dyeing the threads before weaving, so every motif has softly blurred, feathered edges. Designs are bold and flowing, with large almond shapes, teardrop and flame forms, pomegranates, jagged blossoms, stripes and zigzag bands in saturated jewel colours of ruby red, magenta, saffron yellow, indigo, emerald green and black, outlined by thin white lines on a deep ground. Some cloth is shiny and light, some blends silk and cotton for a matte feel. Natural dyes make colours glow but sit a little uneven. Robes, scarves and cushions.'),
('Rishtan Ceramics','Russia and Eastern Europe','traditional to present','ceramics','In the style of Rishtan Ceramics, warm, rustic, sunlit, homely hand thrown pottery in turquoise and blue. Simple, generous rounded forms such as wide shallow dishes and round bowls. The surface has a milky white slip under a clear glaze giving a soft sheen and a faint pale turquoise glow, then painted freehand in turquoise, dark cobalt blue and chocolate brown. Patterns include flowers, branches, pomegranates and pitchers with swirling leafy borders and a central rosette, tiny dotted lines and fine hatching. Some have one calm motif such as a bird or sprig in the middle. Slightly uneven painted lines give life. Arranged on a round cloth with tea, nuts and flatbread.'),
('Kenya Airways','Africa','2000s-present','airlines','In the style of Kenya Airways, warm, hospitable, proud, bright and savannah-like identity in red, white and black. A white body with the name in black italic capitals along the forward body and a bright red tail carrying a stylised letter inside a circle, in white and black. Older schemes run four bands of red, green, black and white along the body in the national flag colours. Engines are red or white, with a small flag near the front. Interiors use red and charcoal seats with white head covers, grey carpets and woven motifs. Crew wear red uniforms with black and white scarves and neat caps. Red against clear blue sky.'),
('Castle Lager','Africa','1950s-present','drinks','In the style of Castle Lager, sociable, relaxed, sunny, outdoorsy heraldic design. Brown glass with a cream, gold and green label bearing a fortress of crenellated towers and a flag inside an oval seal above the name in strong capitals. Glossy green or silver surfaces carry the castle device and a strip of gold. A lighter version uses green with a colour changing cold indicator. Imagery features open fires, sports fields, jazz clubs, street scenes and dusty plains, with beer poured with a creamy head. Crates are yellow plastic with black and red logos. Amber, green, gold and cream.'),
('Da Gama Textiles Three Cats','Africa','19th century to present','textiles','In the style of Da Gama Textiles, traditional, cheerful, communal, crisp and deeply colourful printed cotton. A stiff starched cloth with a papery finish, printed with all-over repeating patterns that look like intricate engraving. The classic colour is indigo blue with white discharged motifs, alongside chocolate brown, deep red, plum, teal and mustard. Motifs are small geometric diamonds, squares, circles, stripes, flowers, paisleys and tiny dotted trellis designs, finely detailed and very regular. The reverse is a flat solid colour with small printed marks. Garments have full A-line skirts, panels sewn side by side and braid and ribbon edging. The cloth holds sharp creases and shows a faint white chalky bloom along folds.'),
('Basotho Blankets','Africa','late 19th century to present','textiles','In the style of Basotho Blankets, proud, heritage-rich, mountain-chilled wrap design. Heavy, tightly woven wool with a soft nap, rectangular, with fringed ends and a plain selvage. Patterns are bold and geometric, with wide stripes, large diamonds, squares, stylised leaf shapes, flowers and crowned shields. Classic combinations include cream and mustard with dark stripes, burgundy and navy blocks, a bold gold and black chevron, and a crown pattern in blue, red and cream. Colours are strong and earthy, with ochre, maroon, navy blue, forest green, black and cream. Worn draped and pinned at the shoulder with a large safety pin, against rocky highlands in cool light.'),
('Ardmore Ceramic Art','Africa','1990s-present','ceramics','In the style of Ardmore Ceramic Art, witty, lush, whimsical, tropical and highly decorative hand sculpted ceramics. Exuberant, playful forms covered with sculpted wild animals such as big cats, striped grazers, monkeys, snakes and birds that climb handles, perch on lids or curl around spouts. Surfaces are a dense riot of dots, lines and leafy patterns in bright glossy colours, including cobalt, emerald, orange, purple, turquoise, red and gold, with iridescent scales and shimmering lustres. Flowers and vines twist across bodies in fine relief. Edges are outlined in dark. Every piece looks like a miniature jungle, bursting with colour and detail.'),
('Kazuri','Africa','1970s-present','jewellery','In the style of Kazuri, joyful, earthy, handmade, colourful and sunny glazed clay design. Hand rolled and shaped pieces, slightly unique and irregular, in round balls, discs, short tubes, cones, ovals, chunky cylinders and tiny seeds, with smooth glass-like surfaces and a visible hole. Colours include cobalt blue, cherry red, mustard yellow, forest green, turquoise, terracotta orange, black, white and speckled earthy brown. Some are hand-painted with swirls, dots, stripes and zigzags in contrasting glaze. They are strung chunky and often mixed in many colours on cotton thread or leather cord, in long ropes and multiple strands. Matching speckled glaze appears on simple rounded vessels.'),
('EgyptAir','Africa','1970s-2000s','airlines','In the style of EgyptAir, stately, ancient, desert-sunny and glowing identity of lapis blue, gold and red. A white body with a deep blue and gold tail carrying a golden falcon figure in a flowing wing-spread pose with a red head, blue feathers and a gold backdrop. The name appears in Latin and Arabic script in dark blue on the forward body. An older scheme has a warm band of red, gold and orange swirling around the window line and engines, giving a sunset glow. Interiors use blue and gold seats with geometric motifs, pale wood trim and a gold emblem. Crew wear smart navy with a hat or scarf in gold.'),
('Ethiopian Airlines','Africa','1990s-present','airlines','In the style of Ethiopian Airlines, welcoming, proud, highland-bright and colourful identity. A pale grey and white body with a grey lower belly and a flowing band of green, yellow and red lines sweeping up toward the tail. A deep green tail carries a yellow and red stylised bird or wing emblem. The name is shown in a native script and Latin capitals in dark green. Interiors feature green seats with woven patterned cloth in red and gold, white head covers and wood panels. Crew uniforms are green, yellow and red with white woven cotton shawls trimmed in coloured borders. Posters repeat the three colour bands as flowing ribbons. Green, gold and red against clear blue sky.'),
('Royal Air Maroc','Africa','1990s-present','airlines','In the style of Royal Air Maroc, warm, hospitable, ornate and sunny identity of red and green geometry. A white body with a vivid red tail carrying a green five pointed star inside a round white emblem, and a slim green and red stripe along the windows. The name appears in Latin and Arabic script in bold dark red on the forward body. Interiors use deep red and green fabrics, tile-inspired geometric patterns in white and blue and brass accents. Crew wear smart dark red with a fine scarf and decorative pin. Imagery shows blue skies over terracotta walls, tilework in blue, green and white and palm trees. Carved latticework repeats an eight pointed star.'),
('Tusker Lager','Africa','1920s-present','drinks','In the style of Tusker Lager, communal, sunny, savannah, relaxed and proud design in red, gold, black and cream. A cream and red label with an upright elephant head in profile with long curved tusks, drawn in bold black ink, above the name in strong capitals. Gold foil wraps the neck, and cans and crates use red, gold and black with the same emblem. Walls are decorated with big hand painted logos and slogans in bold yellow and red sign-painter lettering. Photos show friends around wooden tables beneath thatch with grilled meat, on dusty roadsides. Stacked crates, coasters and plastic stools repeat the emblem in bold black on bright red.'),
('Sapporo Brewery','East Asia','1970s-present','drinks','In the style of Sapporo Brewery, crisp, masculine, social, evening-lit and no-nonsense lager design with a star emblem. Tall slim forms in matte black with a bold gold star and name, or silver with a red star in a circle, or cream and gold labels with thin ruled borders, and deep green with gold edging for special editions. The star is drawn in a crisp geometric outline, centred, with a wordmark in strong serif or slab capitals. Silver foil wraps large formats. The beer is golden with a thick white foam head. Photography shows frosted mugs in a small pub with grilled skewers and paper lanterns. Black, gold, red and silver.'),
('Los Castillo','Latin America','1950s-60s','silver','In the style of Los Castillo, mid-century Mexican modernist metalwork. Heavy hand-hammered forms with sculptural animal shapes like long-necked birds, seahorses, pelicans and fish whose bodies swell into smooth rounded volumes. Surfaces are bright polished metal with a warm slightly rippled hammered texture, set off by chunky cabochon inlays of deep green banded stone, blue lapis and azurite pressed flush into the metal. Chunky links and panels in silver married with copper and brass form interlocking geometry, stepped-fret and feathered-serpent motifs abstracted into bold simple shapes with strong negative space. Handles and feet are cast as stylised beaks, tails and fins. Festive, organic and luxurious, with a slightly imperfect handmade finish and visible tool marks.'),
('Dona Rosa Barro Negro','Latin America','1950s-present','ceramics','In the style of Dona Rosa black pottery, hand-built vessels with a deep, mirror-like metallic black sheen. Clay is shaped by hand on a turning plate with no wheel, so forms are softly rounded and slightly asymmetrical, with tall jars, round bellies, narrow necks, lidded forms and playful figure shapes. The surface is rubbed with a smooth stone before firing in smoke, giving a silky gunmetal-to-jet shine with soft grey matte patches where the burnish is lighter. Decoration is restrained, with applied clay flowers, rosettes, twisted ropes, small handles, delicate pierced lacework openwork and fine incised lines. Unpainted pieces stay monochrome black or silver-grey. Earthy, sculptural and quietly elegant, an ancient shape language with a polished modern gleam, on plain pale backgrounds.'),
('Jacobo y Maria Angeles Workshop','Latin America','1990s-present','folk art','In the style of the Angeles family workshop, joyful, hallucinatory, highly saturated carved and painted folk art. Light soft wood is hand-carved into lively mythical creatures, often with a human face or braided hair on an animal body, caught mid-action while flying, scratching or leaping. After a smooth base coat, the whole body is covered in intricate fine-line ornament in vivid colours of magenta, turquoise, saffron yellow, orange, leaf green and black, in dense repeating patterns of dots, scrolls, flowers, plants, stepped geometric motifs and ancient temple-wall designs. Eyes are large and glossy, tongues and claws picked out in contrasting hues. Light satin finish, with every surface patterned and nothing left blank.'),
('Tenango Otomi Embroidery','Latin America','1960s-present','textiles','In the style of Tenango embroidery, folk, cheerful, playful and slightly naive fantastical animal and plant scenes stitched on cloth. A plain white or cream base, sometimes black, red or blue, filled edge to edge with flat, outlined figures. Motifs are large stylised birds, deer, rabbits, horses, lizards, butterflies and fish, mixed with lush curling flowers, leaves, trees and tiny dots, arranged symmetrically or in mirrored pairs around a central tree. Colours are saturated and not realistic, with sunny yellow, grass green, cobalt blue, hot pink, orange, red and purple, often one hue per figure or striped bands within one animal. Dense, tight stitching with thick coloured thread gives a slightly raised, filled-in look with bold dark outlines.'),
('Wixarika Huichol Beadwork','Latin America','1960s-present','folk art','In the style of Wixarika Huichol beadwork, ceremonial imagery rendered in dense blazing colour. Tiny glass beads are pressed one by one into a layer of wax and resin over carved forms, leaving a shining mosaic surface with a slightly bumpy glittering texture. Flat panels use thick coloured wool pressed into wax in tight spiralling lines that follow each shape like contour maps. Motifs are deer, maize, cactus buttons, scorpions, five-petalled flowers, sun faces, rain clouds and diamond-backed snake bodies, with zigzag lines radiating from animals. The palette is neon-bright and contrasting, fuchsia, turquoise, lime green, electric blue, orange, yellow, red and black with white outlines, filled completely so no background shows. Psychedelic, symmetrical, intricate and intensely handmade, like a jewelled devotional object.'),
('Granado Pharmacias','Latin America','1870s-present','cosmetics','In the style of Granado, nostalgic, refined, slightly aristocratic nineteenth-century apothecary design. Simple old-fashioned packaging with glass bottles with cork or screw stoppers, frosted jars, tin boxes and paper-wrapped bars. Labels are cream, white, pale pink or soft green paper with a thin double-line border, centred oval cartouches, fine ornamental scrollwork and curling flourishes, with elegant serif and decorative Victorian display lettering in deep burgundy, bottle green, navy or gold. Wrappers carry tiny repeating floral and botanical prints and sometimes a small crowned crest. Settings are dark polished wood cabinets, glass-fronted shelves, marble counters and tiled floors in black and white or terracotta. Muted pastel and old-gold accents with restrained, tidy typography.'),
('Varig','Latin America','1960s-90s','airlines','In the style of Varig, clean, optimistic, glamorous jet-age livery. A polished bare-metal lower body with a white upper body separated by a thin navy-blue cheatline along the windows, with the name in large dark blue capitals in a clean wide sans-serif above them. The tail is a vivid royal or cobalt blue field carrying a large circular compass rose emblem in white and gold with dark rays around a central disc. A later scheme becomes a gold-yellow rose on a deep blue belly, engines and tail. A small flag sits near the rear door with a thin italic script word. Earlier schemes show a winged figure in a black circle and a bold black nose stripe. Lots of reflective silver metal.'),
('Wayuu Taya','Latin America','1990s-present','bags','In the style of Wayuu crocheted bags, handmade, tropical, energetic and slightly raw design. Soft round-bottomed cylinder or bucket forms crocheted in a tight single-strand spiral so the fabric is dense and slightly stiff, with a flat circular base and a flat wide strap. A top band and strap in one solid colour contrast with a body covered in large bold geometric designs. Patterns are repeating diamonds, zigzags, stepped squares, crosses, labyrinth-like meanders and stripes in thick yarn. The palette is joyful and high-contrast, hot pink, turquoise, lemon yellow, orange, red, royal blue and lime green against black, white or cream, often with a gradient or striped panel. Braided drawstrings with large tassels, twisted rope handles with pompoms and visibly wavy lines and woollen texture.'),
('Centro de Textiles Tradicionales del Cusco','Latin America','1990s-present','textiles','In the style of the Andean weaving cooperative of Cusco, rich, rustic, rhythmic and symmetrical hand-woven textiles in natural dyed wool. Long narrow bands and square cloths in slightly fuzzy hand-spun yarn. The tight weave shows crisp horizontal stripes of plain colour alternating with dense patterned bands of diamonds, zigzag lines, small stepped figures, birds, animals, flowers inside diamonds, meandering lines and tiny geometric motifs, reversible on both sides. Colours are earthy plant-dye shades, deep indigo and sky blues, cochineal reds, pinks and purples, yellow-greens, mustard, walnut brown, cream and charcoal, with regional palettes such as maroon with white or red with green. Edges are finished with braided cords and tassels. A precise ancient textile language in warm natural tones.'),
('Chulucanas Ceramics','Latin America','1980s-present','ceramics','In the style of Chulucanas pottery, minimalist, tactile, graphic and folk-modern ceramics with smoky resist decoration. Smooth rounded thin-walled vessels with softly bulging bodies, bottle necks and plump shapes, polished to a glossy sheen. Decoration comes from painting liquid clay slip over areas that stay light, then smoke blackens the bare areas, giving crisp contrasts of cream, orange-tan, chocolate brown and glossy black. Patterns are polka-dot spots, tight rows of dots, checkerboards, stripes, spirals, wavy lines, stepped angles and little fish or leaf motifs, often in two colours only, black on tan or tan on black. Some pieces are smoked solid black or painted in several earth colours. Like contemporary sculpture from an ancient workshop.'),
('Habanos Cohiba','Latin America','1960s-present','cigars','In the style of Cohiba, severe, luxurious, quiet, exclusive and masculine tobacco-product design. A narrow black band with bold yellow-gold geometric lettering in angular, jagged capitals inspired by a carved ancestral mask, with a yellow and black chequered pattern inside the main letters. A smaller white and gold secondary band sits beside it. Boxes are flat black or dark brown, with rich lacquer, clean edges, gold foil embossing, a matte black label and a hologram sticker. Contents show smooth, shiny, dark oily brown leaf with fine veins, wrapped in thin cedar sheets, in a deep red and brown glow. A restrained palette of black, yellow, dark green and cedar.'),
('Havana Club','Latin America','1930s-present','spirits','In the style of Havana Club, warm, rhythmic, nostalgic and tropical old-city street-art flavour. Tall squared-shoulder clear glass with a sturdy cork and small neck tag, filled with amber or golden spirit. The label is cream or ivory paper with an aged, slightly weathered look, a big ornate nineteenth-century cigar-box-style cartouche with a gold and red border, a small oval vignette of a fortress and a colonial tower, and lettering in tall wood-type capitals and rounded script. Contemporary versions add colourful screen-printed illustration in saturated flat inks of red, blue, yellow and green, with musicians, dancers, palm trees, vintage cars and skyline. Metallic foil and ribbed stamping on silver and gold labels. Faded colonial palette of mint green, terracotta, sun yellow, turquoise and sepia.'),
('ICAIC Cuban Film Posters','Latin America','1960s-70s','graphic design','In the style of the Cuban film institute poster studio, vibrant, witty, politically charged and strongly handmade silkscreen posters. A few flat, saturated colours in layers with no gradients, bright red, yellow, cobalt blue, orange, green, pink and black, laid down one screen at a time on cheap rough paper with slightly uneven edges and visible misregistration. Imagery is bold, simplified and symbolic, such as a giant eye, a cut-out head, a hand, a skeleton, a face split into colour planes or a single object enlarged to fill the sheet, with playful surreal collage-like juxtapositions and sharp cut-out edges. Lettering is hand-drawn, chunky, irregular, sometimes stencil-like or distorted to match the theme, and sits in blocks of solid colour. Pop art, psychedelia and geometric constructivism blended with satire.'),
('Havanna Alfajores','Latin America','1940s-present','confectionery','In the style of Havanna, friendly, sweet, nostalgic seaside design in a trustworthy clean cream and blue palette. Deep turquoise-blue or royal blue and white schemes with warm cream, a large rounded white script logo like a flowing signature over navy, slim gold or silver details and a small orange rising-sun mark. Packaging uses soft rounded rectangular shapes, shiny foil, tins and maritime references such as a seaside town and small gulls. Treats are round, glossy dark chocolate or white icing over soft pale layers. Spaces are warm wood-and-brass, with dark wood counters, tall windows, beige marble tables and lamps with amber light.'),
('Pomaire Potters','Latin America','19th century-present','ceramics','In the style of the Pomaire potters, earthy, handmade, humble and warm rustic terracotta. Heavy, thick-walled forms, unglazed or lightly burnished, in warm reddish-brown to dark grey-brown clay with a smooth matte surface that darkens with use. Shapes are chunky and round, with two ear handles, wide shallow bowls, lidded casseroles, jugs and plates. Plump little animal figures, small pinched and moulded folk figures and a three-legged pig money box with a slot add charm. Some are painted with simple flat colours or white slip dots and stripes, others left plain with finger marks and uneven rims. Kiln smoke gives mottled black clouds and variations. Stacked on rough wooden shelves in an adobe market.'),
('Guna Mola Cooperatives','Latin America','20th century-present','textiles','In the style of Guna reverse-appliqued mola panels, graphic, rhythmic, vibrant and strongly handmade design. Two to seven layers of thin cotton in contrasting solid colours, the top layer cut away in curving shapes so the layers beneath peek through, with edges turned under and hemmed with tiny nearly invisible stitches. The design fills the whole panel with energetic horror vacui of tightly packed shapes in parallel concentric outlines, like a thick-lined labyrinth, depicting birds, fish, sea turtles, flowers, masks and abstract geometry. Colours are bright, fully saturated and placed in bold contrast, red against orange, black against yellow, green against hot pink, blue against white. Small slits, dots, zigzag borders and lattice patterns add detail. Flat and symmetrical like stained glass.'),
('Bacardi','Latin America','1860s-present','spirits','In the style of Bacardi, festive, tropical, confident and slightly retro heraldic design. The central symbol is a black bat with outspread wings seen from the front, drawn in a bold, simple, slightly gothic silhouette with a small head, set inside a red, white and black label. Labels are bright, clean white or cream with a red, black or gold border, big black block lettering, a small crest and a tiny red wax-like seal. Premium versions use deeper amber, gold-foil edging and aged cream labels with ornate serif lettering. Dark oak and iron hoops appear in the background. Advertising shows sunny beaches, palm fronds and bright red umbrellas. An Art Deco tower clad in blue-and-white geometric tiles with a stepped crown.'),
('Haitian Metal Drum Art','Latin America','20th century-present','folk art','In the style of the Haitian metalworkers of Croix-des-Bouquets, raw, intricate, spiritual and richly patterned flat sculpture cut from recycled steel drums. Panels are flattened, drawn with chalk, then chiselled and punched so the line work appears as cut-through openings and raised ridges. Subjects are a tree of life, mermaids, birds, fish, sun faces, spirits with elaborate headdresses and crosses, drawn with symmetrical swirling leaves, scales, dotted outlines, hearts and curling vines. The metal is left dark grey and rust-brown, sometimes polished to rough silver with burn marks, or hand-painted in bright enamel like red, yellow and turquoise. Shapes are oval, round or irregular with ragged cut edges, sometimes bent into three-dimensional forms. A rugged industrial material turned into delicate lace.'),
('Acoma Pueblo Pottery','North America','20th century-present','ceramics','In the style of Acoma Pueblo potters, crisp, disciplined, optical and graceful extremely thin-walled hand-coiled ceramics with fine-line painting. Rounded vessels with high shoulders and small mouths, and low wide shapes, with a very fine white slip surface that is smooth, matte and chalk-like. The walls are paper thin. Decoration is painted with a fine brush in black and rusty orange or red-brown on the creamy white ground, in dense precise geometric bands. Motifs are fine-line lattices and hatching, interlocking triangles, birds, rainbows, stepped clouds, animals with a heart line and scrolls, with bands wrapping horizontally around the shoulder and neck and tidy empty zones at the base. Unglazed, powdery, with slightly brown tonal variations from the fire. Like delicate op-art on earthenware.'),
('San Ildefonso Pueblo Pottery','North America','1920s-present','ceramics','In the style of San Ildefonso Pueblo black-on-black pottery, sleek, dark, formal, sculptural and timeless. Hand-coiled, perfectly symmetrical forms with a rounded, full body, a marked shoulder angle, a short narrow neck and a slightly flattened rim. The whole surface is burnished to a glass-smooth gloss and smoke-fired to a deep jet black. Designs are painted in clay slip which stays matte after polishing, so the pattern shows as flat dull black against a shining black field, visible only as light shifts across it. A wide band around the shoulder holds a coiled horned water serpent, rain clouds, steps, lightning zigzags, mountains and bird tracks. Some pieces are carved through the surface, others red or sienna with matte-and-polish contrasts. Perfect balance.'),
('Toadlena Trading Post Weavings','North America','1900s-1930s','textiles','In the style of the Toadlena Two Grey Hills weavings, calm, earthy, refined and architectural natural-wool tapestry. Flat-woven very tightly and finely in a rectangular format with a dense, almost smooth surface. Colours come only from undyed wool carded and blended, so the palette is creamy white, light and dark grey, tan, camel, chocolate brown and jet black, with no bright dye. The design is a symmetrical central geometric field with diamonds, stepped zigzags, concentric rectangles and terraced crosses, framed by a plain border and a crisp inner outline, with small tapering corner details and often a single dark stripe on the edge. Balanced, precise and optical, with crisp straight edges and no fringe. Like a desert landscape abstracted into straight lines.'),
('West Baffin Eskimo Cooperative','North America','1950s-present','graphic design','In the style of the Cape Dorset printmaking and carving cooperative, quiet, northern, graphic and dignified design with a simple, bold and direct line. Prints show simple powerful animals and spirit figures with big expressive eyes and feathers drawn as repeating curved shapes, printed in flat ink on thin pale cream or white handmade paper. The ink is deep black, with blue-grey, ochre, red-orange, green and teal appearing as flat blocks, with a soft grain from the stone and a subtle ridge around each shape, often with generous empty paper space around them. Sculpture is smooth, rounded, polished dark green-grey or black stone in heavy, compact forms of animals, figures and hybrid creatures.'),
]
